WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
Spanish has no "-er"
ending for "taller".

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.570
It says "more tall" instead:
Ana es más alta que Luis.

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.170
"Ana is taller than Luis.

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.170
" So Sam follows the same
pattern for "This book is better.

5
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.790
" He writes: Este libro es más bueno.

6
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.970
In English, "more good" sounds odd.

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.930
But does it work in Spanish?

8
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.370
In this mission, you'll build
comparisons with more, less,

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.220
and as tall as.

10
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.710
You'll see which little word means
"than", and which means "as".

11
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.890
Then you'll go one step further,
to the most and the least.

12
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.050
Your mission: find out whether
Sam's más bueno passes the test.
